From 60c5016b7661cd604917e7a5990a6f38bcdf9b90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:10:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The reticle's own line: GetReticlePoint, the aim's circle on
 it, and the twenty-sixth round

The reticle is drawn in the middle of the screen, but the aim's point was found along the server's
guess at it: a line from the hero's eye (1.9 yd up, 0.75 right) along the view, parallel to the
camera's line and 0.25 yd under it (the camera sits over the pivot), so the circle and the reticle
could disagree by up to a few yards on the ground.

Now, while the aiming camera is up, the line is the camera's own through the middle of the screen,
from where it passes the hero (nothing between the camera and the hero is aimed at), to the first
ground, wall or doodad. `GetReticlePoint()` returns that point (WoW x, y, z) and whether something
stands between the hero's hands and it (`blocked`: a shot from behind cover hits the cover); the
add-on sends the point with each shot and the server fires there from the hands. The aim's circle
lies on the same line. Without the aiming camera, the old line. `HasActionCombat()` says 26 (24 and
25 are the Mage's).
